| Detection Metadata                                                                    |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Detection Name    : Registry Run Key Persistence Modification                         |
| Detection ID      : DET-005                                                           |
| MITRE Tactic      : Persistence                                                       |
| MITRE Technique   : T1547.001 — Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder                   |
| Severity          : High                                                              |
| Data Sources      : Sysmon Event 13 (RegistryValueSet)                               |

================================================================================
PRIMARY QUERY — Run Key Write Detection
================================================================================

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
EventID=13
(
    TargetObject="*\\CurrentVersion\\Run\\*"
    OR TargetObject="*\\CurrentVersion\\RunOnce\\*"
    OR TargetObject="*\\CurrentVersion\\RunOnceEx\\*"
    OR TargetObject="*\\CurrentVersion\\RunServices\\*"
)
NOT Image IN (
    "*\\msiexec.exe",
    "*\\setup.exe",
    "*\\install*.exe",
    "*\\Dropbox*.exe",
    "*\\OneDrive.exe",
    "*\\Teams.exe"
)
| eval detection="Registry Run Key — Persistence Write"
| eval mitre="T1547.001"
| eval severity="High"
| eval suspicious_value=if(
    like(Details, "%Temp%") OR like(Details, "%AppData%") OR like(Details, "%-enc%"),
    "HIGH RISK — suspicious path or encoded content",
    "MEDIUM — review writing process and value"
  )
| table _time, ComputerName, User, Image, TargetObject, Details, suspicious_value
| sort -_time

================================================================================
KNOWN FALSE POSITIVES
================================================================================
- Software installers (msiexec, setup.exe — excluded above)
- Common autostart apps: Dropbox, OneDrive, Teams, Zoom (add to exclusion list)
- Corporate software deployed via Group Policy
